# Julia versions CI passes to setup-julia. One version per line.
# Write the version itself (1.13, ~1.14.0-0, nightly). Do not use min / max.
# Job titles use a display label. For 1.13 and nightly the label is the
# version string. The 1.14 prerelease line keeps the version string
# ~1.14.0-0 (setup-julia: alpha, then beta, then rc, then 1.14.x, below
# 1.15) and the display label 1.14-pre
# (`Pkg.test (1.14-pre, ubuntu-latest, x64)`).
# When a required version changes, change the job names and the main
# ruleset in that PR. 1.14-pre is not a required check.
#
# First stable line: maintained stable, Project.toml julia floor. Required.
#   Pkg.test, Aqua, JETLS, Documenter, bake, E2E kit parent, GHCR worker.
# 1.14 prerelease line (~1.14.0-0, display 1.14-pre): continue-on-error.
#   JETLS, Aqua, and Ubuntu Pkg.test on heavy pull requests (including
#   ordinary ones), on main, on CI weekly, and on a version cut.
#   macOS and WSL2 Pkg.test and Aqua on CI weekly only.
#   No E2E or docs.
# `nightly` (Julia master): continue-on-error.
#   Ubuntu Pkg.test and Aqua on main, CI weekly, and a version cut.
#   macOS and WSL2 on CI weekly only.
#   No JETLS, E2E, or docs. Do not add another stable line.
#
# JETLS runs on the stable line and on the 1.14 prerelease line.
# nightly runs no JETLS. If the stable runtime is outside JETLS's range,
# add another stable line and job.
1.13
~1.14.0-0
nightly
# E2E mismatch only (setup --juliaup). Not a test version.
JULIA_E2E_MISMATCH_CHANNEL=1.12
